David Justiss wrote:
>  - trap doors separate me from my pet

Yah, that's annoying.

>  - my pet eats while I'm getting killed  (I write Elbereth but it's just
> not very reliable when written in the dust)

You can and should write elbereth multiple times in the dust for a more
consistant result. Write 1 elbereth in the dust each turn for a few
turns (adding to the current engraving). 3 usually does the trick for
me.

>  - my pet just doesn't always attack the monsters that are attacking me
> (even when he's not eating)

There are rules as to when the pet will attack: if it has enough
health, if it is strong enough to attack the opponent, etc. You can
check your pet's health with a stethoscope if you have one, or cast a
healing spell on it if you can.

>  - my pet keeps getting himself killed by the watch captain

Yeah, you have to protect your pet from attacking the watch captain -
it will almost always die if you don't help it in some way. It should
be able to handle all the normal watchmen, however.

> ..oh stinkin.. I just realized my mistake in the situation detailed
> above.  I could've just bought the magic whistle which is cheap and then
> I take control of my pet's stealing.  ug

Yep, a magic whistle or leash help a lot with stealing. Pet picks up
item, blow whistle (while you're standing in the doorway). eventually
the pet drops the item, go pick it up, stand in the doorway, and blow
the whistle until the pet is back in the store. Wait for it to pick up
another item, rinse and repeat. Leash is the same way, but when the pet
picks up an item quickly walk out of the store before the pet has a
chance to drop the item.

I rarely try stealing if i don't have one of those items (magic
whistle, leash)- not that it can't be done but it's just that i usually
don't have the patience. It helps in these situations if you have a
tripe ration/meatball to increase your pets tameness.

> anyway, you get the idea that my pet rarely does what I want him to.

Yep, pets can be frustrating especially without a magic whistle/leash.

